 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** HDR color $c_{hi}$ at view direction $d=(\theta, \phi)$, exposure time $\Delta t$, and SH coefficients $k$.
-*   **Output:** LDR color $c_{li}$.
+*   **Input:** HDR color $c_{hi}$ at view direction $d=(\theta, \phi)$, exposure time $\Delta t$, and SH coefficients $k$ [S1].
+*   **Output:** LDR color $c_{li}$ [S1].
 
 **Data Structures:**
-*   **SH Coefficients ($k$):** A set of coefficients $k = \{k_{lm} \mid 0 \le l \le L, -l \le m \le l\} \in \mathbb{R}^{(L+1)^2 \times 3}$. Each $k_{lm} \in \mathbb{R}^3$ corresponds to the RGB components. $L$ is the SH degree [S1].
-*   **Tone Mapper ($g_\theta$):** An MLP architecture per RGB channel consisting of:
-    1.  Fully Connected (fc) layer.
-    2.  ReLU activation.
-    3.  Fully Connected (fc) layer.
-    4.  Sigmoid activation [S1].
+*   **SH Coefficients ($k$):** A set of coefficients $k = \{k_{lm} \mid 0 \le l \le L, -l \le m \le l\} \in \mathbb{R}^{(L+1)^2 \times 3}$ [S1]. Each $k_{lm} \in \mathbb{R}^3$ corresponds to the RGB components [S1]. $L$ is the SH degree [S1].
+*   **Tone Mapper ($g_\theta$):** An MLP architecture per RGB channel consisting of: 1. Fully Connected (fc) layer, 2. ReLU activation, 3. Fully Connected (fc) layer, 4. Sigmoid activation [S1].
 
 **Steps:**
-
